{"id": "EUVD-2026-81809", "enisaUuid": "ca59c592-87c9-3f95-b800-da3d46d32c77", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nubi: Fix rollback for explicit UBI device numbers\n\nubi_init_attach() rolls back module initialization failures by scanning\nubi_devices[0..i-1], where i is the mtd= parameter index. That assumes\nthe parameter index matches the UBI device number.\n\nThat assumption is not true when mtd= specifies an explicit ubi_num. A\nsuccessfully attached device can be stored at a higher ubi_devices[]\nslot, and a later failure can miss it during rollback.\n\nScan the full ubi_devices[] array and detach by the actual array index,\nmatching the way UBI devices are stored.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83c978921688af40dcab6db74882d1ff9b0b765c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b92e66ec6dd8019e8efb2a568ef7c967c5a18c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4417ab6ecad01cf2d01045ef8104c95a66b0e893", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/552e565ed8846e7db143e4a6bdf3f5677453c686", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9754f049d5f1945d4c691d1f52824eb8daf8f9be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3f7e58189bc222971ddc860f1716f37e51ba996", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87b3da4acb860605643ebee312178f13b20744cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b0a6b554e12a97f9771a9a9f4ea1f5457373c73"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90216", "GHSA-98x6-774g-8659"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17517793-be8a-3bae-8b6e-c50643b45e44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83ff59a066637a6c28844bbf43009459408240f4 <4417ab6ecad01cf2d01045ef8104c95a66b0e893"}, {"id": "43b85c44-99be-3796-9b72-8394074dc87c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "5d4e8031-aaf2-31dd-9970-d01a623ef5a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend